@startuml
' Figure 14.6  Speculative decoding
' Reading order: top to bottom. A small draft model guesses four
' tokens; the large model checks all four in one pass, keeps the run it
' agrees with, and supplies the next token itself, so output matches
' what the large model alone would produce. From serving.speculative.
!include plantuml-theme.puml
participant "Draft\nmodel" as D <<ops>>
participant "Target\nmodel" as T <<model>>
D -> D : Guess 4 tokens, cheap steps
D -> T : "rebook" "on" "UA" "1432"
T -> T : One pass over all four
T -[$FAIL]> D : Keep 3, reject "1432"
T -> D : Its own token: "1438"
note over D, T : 4 tokens for 1 large pass
@enduml
